* Power-up stability in the gain -1 network at tt / 1.8 V / 27 C: VDD ramps
* from 0 to 1.8 V in 5 ms and holds for 2 ms.  Prints the peak-to-peak of Vod
* and of the output common mode over the last 1 ms of the hold; anything well
* above a few millivolts means the amplifier oscillates.  Grading also ramps
* down, uses 10 ms ramps, adds supply surges and runs at -40 and 125 C.
* Run with `ngspice -b testbench/tb_powerup_tt.spi`.
.lib "/opt/sky130/continuous/sky130.lib.spice" tt
.include "/app/circuit.spi"
.options reltol=1e-4 abstol=1e-12 vntol=1e-6 method=gear
.temp 27
VDD vdd 0 PWL(0 0 5m 1.8)
VSS vss 0 0
IBIAS vdd ibias 10u
VCM vcm 0 0.9
R1 vcm inp 100k
R2 inp outn 100k
R3 vcm inn 100k
R4 inn outp 100k
XDUT vss ibias vdd vcmpin inp inn outp outn fd_opamp
RVCM vcm vcmpin 1k
RLP outp vcm 1meg
CLP outp 0 2p
RLN outn vcm 1meg
CLN outn 0 2p
.control
set noaskquit
tran 1u 7m 0 1u
let vod = v(outp) - v(outn)
let vocm = 0.5 * (v(outp) + v(outn))
meas tran vod_pp_v PP vod FROM=6m TO=7m
meas tran vocm_pp_v PP vocm FROM=6m TO=7m
quit
.endc
.end
